{"id": "EUVD-2026-96999", "enisaUuid": "d7bac00e-5358-3d01-a3ca-a6e7369b6036", "description": "hyper-mcp through 0.8.3 contains an improper signature verification vulnerability that allows attackers to load malicious WebAssembly plugins because cosign_verify_args() accepts any signer identity and OIDC issuer by default. Attackers controlling a plugin image reference can sign a malicious image with a free Sigstore keyless certificate to execute plugins with configured host, filesystem, and environment capabilities.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T13:25:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:35:43", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/hyper-mcp-oci-signature-manifest-toctou", "https://github.com/hyper-mcp-rs/hyper-mcp/blob/v0.8.3/src/wasm/oci.rs#L157-L190", "https://github.com/hyper-mcp-rs/hyper-mcp/blob/v0.8.3/src/config.rs#L138-L170", "https://github.com/hyper-mcp-rs/hyper-mcp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/hyper-mcp-through-0.8.3-improper-signature-verification-of-oci-webassembly-plugins"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4j25-h357-wg62", "CVE-2026-108699"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e995d2c-fcaa-3ad5-bcc8-b3acd076ec3c", "product": {"name": "hyper-mcp", "vendor": {"name": "hyper-mcp-rs"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.8.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0f651a6d-ce7c-37b3-8a53-f7da70cf9e97", "vendor": {"name": "hyper-mcp-rs"}}], "isExploited": false}